  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skills for Youth Resilience Programme (SYRP) in Mozambique and Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x2018;Skills for Youth Resilience Programme (SYRP) in Mozambique and Zimbabwe&#x2019; project aims for young people to have more financial and personal capacity to minimise the impact of shocks to their wellbeing. The implementing partners are Young Africa Zimbabwe, Young Africa Mozambique, and Young Africa Hub. The objective is the provision of holistic Technical Vocational and Educational Training (TVET), including entrepreneurship and life skills training, to marginalised young people through support for training centres run by local partners. The key activities include a Scholarship Programme; a Microcredit Programme; Improving Post Graduate Supports; and Supporting Outreach Training to rural communities.  Organisational Resilience including Capacity building, and HR support.</narrative>
  </description>
